+# AGENTS.md — Guide for Future Agents
+
+## Repository: benchlib
+Small pure-Python utility library (v0.1.0, Python ≥3.10) used for agent benchmarking.
+
+## Architecture
+Flat single-package layout — no subpackages, no `src/` directory. Two library modules sit at the repo root alongside their tests:
+
+- **`calc.py`** — arithmetic helpers: `add(a, b)`, `sub(a, b)`, `mul(a, b)`, `div(a, b)`. `div` raises `ZeroDivisionError` on `b == 0`.
+- **`textproc.py`** — text helpers: `word_count(text)`, `reverse_words(text)`, `capitalize_words(text)`. All three split on single spaces (`text.split(" ")`).
+
+Supporting files: `pyproject.toml` (project metadata + pytest config, `testpaths = ["."]`), `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `.gitignore` (ignores `__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`, `.pytest_cache/`).
+
+## Running Tests
+From the repo root:
+```
+pip install -e .
+pytest
+```
+Tests live next to the modules they cover (`test_calc.py`, `test_textproc.py`) and are auto-discovered by pytest.
+
+## Known Failing Tests
+Two tests in `test_textproc.py` are **expected to fail** — they document a known bug in `word_count` (it splits on single spaces only, so punctuation and consecutive spaces miscount):
+
+- `test_word_count_punctuation` — `word_count("Hello,  world!!")` returns 4, not 2.
+- `test_word_count_empty` — `word_count("")` returns 1 (empty string), not 0.
+
+Do not "fix" these tests; fix `word_count` in `textproc.py` (e.g. use `re.findall(r"\b\w+\b", text)` or `text.split()`) and the tests will pass. `reverse_words` and `capitalize_words` share the same single-space split and may have edge-case issues too.
+
+## Conventions
+- Pure Python, no external runtime dependencies (pytest is dev-only).
+- Type hints on all public function signatures.
+- Keep modules flat at the repo root unless the project grows a `src/` layout.
